INSERT OR IGNORE INTO categories(name,slug,description,sort_order) VALUES ('Lightsaber Forms','lightsaber-forms','Star Wars / Shared reference library for all seven classical forms.',22),('Force Studies','force-studies','Star Wars / Shared Force lore and comparative philosophy.',23),('Galactic History','galactic-history','Star Wars / Canon and Legends history and research.',24);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'The seven lightsaber forms: reference index','lightsaber-seven-index','A shared lore library for Jedi and Sith. The seven classical forms are Shii-Cho, Makashi, Soresu, Ataru, Shien/Djem So, Niman and Juyo/Vaapad. Their names and detailed classifications are developed across franchise reference works and Legends, with varying degrees of canon confirmation. These lessons describe fictional choreography, philosophy and narrative symbolism, not practical weapon instruction.

Study order: Forms I–VII, followed by comparison and continuity notes.',1 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='lightsaber-forms' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Form I — Shii-Cho: the foundation','lightsaber-form-1','Shii-Cho is traditionally described as the earliest classical lightsaber form, associated with foundational movements and the transition from conventional swords to lightsabers. Its fictional identity emphasizes simplicity, adaptability and basic familiarity with the weapon. In reference lore it is often associated with broad movements and multiple opponents.

Narrative strength: accessibility and versatility. Limitation: less specialization for individual lightsaber duels. Philosophy: foundations matter more than ornament. Kit Fisto is commonly associated with this form in Legends/reference lore. Discussion: why do advanced practitioners return to fundamentals?',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='lightsaber-forms' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Form II — Makashi: precision and economy','lightsaber-form-2','Makashi is the classical dueling-oriented form, associated with elegance, precision and economical movement. Count Dooku''s screen choreography exemplifies its refined fencing-inspired identity. Reference lore contrasts its specialization against other lightsaber wielders with less emphasis on projectile defense.

Narrative strength: composure and precision. Limitation: narrow specialization. Philosophy: control and economy can outperform spectacle. Compare Dooku''s portrayal in Attack of the Clones and Revenge of the Sith. Discussion: when does specialization become rigidity?',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='lightsaber-forms' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Form III — Soresu: patience and defense','lightsaber-form-3','Soresu is associated with sustained defense, restraint and survival under pressure. Obi-Wan Kenobi is its best-known representative in franchise reference lore. Its narrative identity emphasizes patience, conservation and waiting rather than imposing immediate victory.

Narrative strength: endurance and protection. Limitation: defensive success does not necessarily resolve a conflict. Philosophy: refusing to be provoked is a form of agency. Compare Obi-Wan''s character across the prequel trilogy. Discussion: when is restraint wise, and when does it become passivity?',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='lightsaber-forms' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Form IV — Ataru: mobility and expression','lightsaber-form-4','Ataru is associated with acrobatic, Force-assisted choreography and energetic movement. Yoda''s duels in the prequel films illustrate the visual language commonly associated with this form. Reference lore emphasizes mobility and initiative, with demanding energy requirements and environmental limitations.

Narrative strength: adaptability through movement. Limitation: dependence on stamina and space. Philosophy: apparent physical limitations need not define identity. Discussion: how does Yoda''s unexpected movement challenge assumptions about strength?',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='lightsaber-forms' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Form V — Shien and Djem So: response and assertion','lightsaber-form-5','Form V is traditionally divided into Shien and Djem So. Reference lore associates Shien with responding to ranged threats and Djem So with forceful lightsaber dueling. Anakin Skywalker and Darth Vader are frequently associated with Form V, making it an especially useful bridge between Jedi and Sith studies.

Narrative strength: turning pressure into initiative. Limitation: the temptation to rely on force and control. Philosophy: responding to adversity need not mean becoming aggressive. Compare Anakin and Vader''s contrasting portrayals. Discussion: when does assertiveness become domination?',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='lightsaber-forms' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Form VI — Niman: synthesis and balance','lightsaber-form-6','Niman is described in reference lore as an integrative form drawing on earlier traditions, often associated with Jedi who prioritize diplomacy and broader Force studies. It is less narrowly specialized than several other forms. Its identity is synthesis rather than superiority in every discipline.

Narrative strength: flexibility and breadth. Limitation: general competence may not equal specialist mastery. Philosophy: balance requires deliberate integration, not merely compromise. Discussion: compare the value of a generalist with that of a specialist in an academy or community.',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='lightsaber-forms' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Form VII — Juyo and Vaapad: intensity and restraint','lightsaber-form-7','Juyo is traditionally characterized by intensity and unpredictability. Vaapad is a related but distinct development associated with Mace Windu, particularly in Legends and reference material. It should not be treated as a synonym for the Sith or as proof that aggression alone grants mastery.

Narrative strength: intensity and commitment. Limitation: emotional instability and ethical risk are recurring themes. Philosophy: engaging with difficult emotions requires accountability. Compare Windu''s portrayal with the Sith''s use of passion. Discussion: can a tradition acknowledge anger without making anger its governing principle?',0 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='lightsaber-forms' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Shared Force studies: balance, destiny and free will','force-shared-balance','The Force is a fictional metaphysical field connecting life. Jedi and Sith interpret its meaning differently. Balance is a recurring narrative question, not necessarily an equal numerical division between light and dark practitioners. Compare the prophecy in the prequel trilogy, the Mortis arc in The Clone Wars and Luke''s teachings in The Last Jedi.

Study questions: does destiny remove responsibility? Can balance be understood as harmony rather than equal quantities of opposing forces? Separate direct story evidence from philosophical interpretation.',1 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='force-studies' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO threads(category_id,user_id,title,slug,body,pinned) SELECT c.id,u.id,'Shared history: Canon and Legends research guide','galactic-history-guide','Maintain two separate timelines. Current Canon includes the main films and designated contemporary stories; Legends encompasses the former Expanded Universe, including many Old Republic narratives. A character, event or term may exist in both while its details differ.

Begin with the official Star Wars Databank at https://www.starwars.com/databank and the films. For Legends, identify the specific novel, comic or game and its publication context. Record the era, continuity, source and uncertainty for each entry. Do not silently merge incompatible histories.',1 FROM categories c CROSS JOIN users u WHERE c.slug='galactic-history' AND u.username='knightfall' AND u.role='god';